WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.388 --> 00:00:04.671
Unit six. Health Ethics and Decision-Making!

2
00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:10.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:13.097
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:18.167
Today we learn about Health Ethics and Decision-Making. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:24.408
Health ethics. Say it with me. Health ethics!

6
00:00:27.936 --> 00:00:32.736
Informed consent. Say it with me. Informed consent!

7
00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:40.891
Confidentiality. Say it with me. Confidentiality!

8
00:00:44.452 --> 00:00:48.518
Autonomy. Say it with me. Autonomy!

9
00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:56.529
Ethical dilemma. Say it with me. Ethical dilemma!

10
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:03.892
Fairness. Say it with me. Fairness!

11
00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:12.952
Professional responsibility. Say it with me. Professional responsibility!

12
00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:20.769
Moral reasoning. Say it with me. Moral reasoning!

13
00:01:24.281 --> 00:01:41.416
Health ethics includes respecting informed consent and patient confidentiality. Autonomy means respecting a person's right to make their own health decisions. An ethical dilemma often requires fairness, professional responsibility, and careful moral reasoning.

14
00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:44.740
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:45.491 --> 00:01:50.620
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.093
Confidentiality!

17
00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:58.473
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:00.703
Professional responsibility!

19
00:02:01.672 --> 00:02:10.007
Did you know? The promise to keep patients' secrets appears in the ancient Greek Hippocratic Oath, written more than 2,000 years ago.

20
00:02:10.057 --> 00:02:12.252
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:13.493 --> 00:02:23.050
Think and answer. Why might confidentiality be especially important in healthcare?

22
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.250
Great answer!

23
00:02:25.328 --> 00:02:30.951
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
